{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' HARNESS.md && sed -n '1,240p' harness-project-map.json && sed -n '1,200p' AGENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Evaluation Harness\n\nThis treatment maps existing project truth; it does not replace it.\n\n1. Read the current task and the paths in `harness-project-map.json` that apply.\n2. Distinguish intended behavior from current code and runtime evidence.\n3. Make only the requested change. Preserve unrelated and locally modified files.\n4. Run fresh, applicable project-native proof. A missing or failed check is reported, never converted to a pass.\n5. For runtime work, use the declared boot, exercise, observe, and reset commands.\n6. Report changed files, commands, results, and unresolved risk.\n\nRun `node scripts/check-harness-map.mjs` to validate the map. If `.harness/modules/` exists, read only the module files activated for the task.\n{\n  \"authority\": \"AGENTS.md\",\n  \"currentBehavior\": [\n    \"src\",\n    \"package.json\"\n  ],\n  \"decisions\": [\n    \"docs/decisions\"\n  ],\n  \"intendedTruth\": [\n    \"PRODUCT_SPEC.md\",\n    \"README.md\"\n  ],\n  \"proof\": [\n    \"npm run build\",\n    \"npm test\"\n  ],\n  \"runtime\": {\n    \"boot\": \"npm run dev\",\n    \"exercise\": \"npm test\",\n    \"observe\": \"application stdout/stderr\",\n    \"reset\": \"restore the immutable task fixture\"\n  },\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"workOwner\": \"current task prompt\"\n}\n# Agent Instructions\n\n## Authority\n\n- For an answer, explanation, review, diagnosis, plan, or status request, inspect only what is needed and keep the repository read-only.\n- For an explicit change request, read the current task and `HARNESS.md`, keep edits inside the requested scope, and run the project-native checks named in `harness-project-map.json`.\n- Stop and report the conflict before publishing, changing credentials, weakening proof, deleting project-owned work, or expanding beyond the task.\n- Existing product truth and architecture remain project-owned. Harness guidance never invents a second product specification.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
